From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, user32, explorer: Shell.Application's shell commands; CascadeWindows and TileWindows

Shell.Application's shell commands were E_NOTIMPL: MinimizeAll and
UndoMinimizeALL, ToggleDesktop, FileRun, CascadeWindows and the tiles,
ShutdownWindows, Suspend, SetTime, TrayProperties, Open and Explore,
Windows, FindFiles and FindComputer, ControlPanelItem, IsRestricted,
GetSystemInformation, ServiceStart/ServiceStop and CanStartStopService,
AddToRecent, ExplorerPolicy, GetSetting, WindowSwitcher and SearchCommand
(BrowseForFolder ignored its root). Under them, user32's CascadeWindows
and TileWindows were stubs, SHFindFiles was one, and the taskbar ignored
the WM_COMMAND shell commands programs send Windows' taskbar ("Shell
command 419 is not supported").

- user32: CascadeWindows and TileWindows arrange the given windows, or the
  parent's (the desktop's: visible, not minimized, captioned, unowned,
  MDITILE_SKIPDISABLED honoured) in the given rectangle or the work area:
  cascaded down and right a caption apart, the bottom window first, three
  quarters of the area each; tiled side by side (MDITILE_VERTICAL) or one
  above the other (MDITILE_HORIZONTAL), in a grid past three. Maximized
  windows are restored; other programs' windows are moved without waiting
  for them.
- explorer's taskbar carries out the shell commands: Run (401), Cascade
  (403), Tile horizontally/vertically (404/405), Show the desktop (407),
  Date and time (408), Taskbar settings (413), Minimize all (415, 419),
  Undo minimize all (416), Shut down (506).
- Shell.Application sends the taskbar those commands, as Windows' does
  (with direct fallbacks when there is no taskbar); opens and explores
  folders (a path, CSIDL or Folder); Windows gives the ShellWindows
  collection; Suspend sleeps; SetTime and TrayProperties open their
  settings; ControlPanelItem runs control.exe with the item;
  IsRestricted and ExplorerPolicy read the Policies keys (machine, then
  user); GetSystemInformation answers DoubleClickTime, Processor*,
  PhysicalMemoryInstalled, DirectoryServiceAvailable and IsOS_*;
  ServiceStart/Stop start and stop services (persistent: their start
  type too) with the caller's rights; CanStartStopService says whether it
  has them; AddToRecent adds to the recent documents; GetSetting reads the
  SSF_ settings; WindowsSecurity shows the lock screen; WindowSwitcher and
  SearchCommand open Task View and search; ShowBrowserBar shows none;
  EjectPC has nothing to undock; BrowseForFolder takes its root.
- SHFindFiles opens File Explorer at the folder (or This PC) with the
  search box focused: explorer's new "/search[,folder]" option.

Wine's shell32 shelldispatch tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/shelldisp-gate.sh (Xvfb, the shell's desktop: tiling and
cascading, minimize all and undo, the desktop toggle, the Run dialog,
system information, policies, settings, a service's rights, ShellWindows,
a search window). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_ARRANGE (user32/mdi.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_TRAY_COMMANDS (programs/explorer/systray.c).
